1248
00:49:58,720 --> 00:50:03,040
This biological model is what inspired

1249
00:50:00,800 --> 00:50:06,599
the design of artificial neural networks

1250
00:50:03,040 --> 00:50:06,599
in machine learning.

1251
00:50:08,079 --> 00:50:12,720
Here is a simplified view of how neurons

1252
00:50:10,160 --> 00:50:15,760
work. Think of this as the basic flow of

1253
00:50:12,720 --> 00:50:17,599
information in our nervous system.

1254
00:50:15,760 --> 00:50:19,839
Incoming signals, whether from the

1255
00:50:17,599 --> 00:50:22,480
outside world or from other neurons,

1256
00:50:19,839 --> 00:50:24,000
arrive at the dendrites. These dendrites

1257
00:50:22,480 --> 00:50:26,160
act as the input terminals of the

1258
00:50:24,000 --> 00:50:27,839
neuron. They collect all incoming

1259
00:50:26,160 --> 00:50:30,000
information both excitatory and

1260
00:50:27,839 --> 00:50:31,680
inhibitory.

1261
00:50:30,000 --> 00:50:33,440
If the combined strength of these

1262
00:50:31,680 --> 00:50:35,760
signals is strong enough to cross a

1263
00:50:33,440 --> 00:50:37,920
certain threshold, the neuron generates

1264
00:50:35,760 --> 00:50:40,400
an electrical pulse called an action

1265
00:50:37,920 --> 00:50:42,880
potential. This signal travels down the

1266
00:50:40,400 --> 00:50:46,079
axon, the long fiber you see here, and

1267
00:50:42,880 --> 00:50:48,079
moves toward the axon terminals.

1268
00:50:46,079 --> 00:50:49,760
At the axon terminals, the neuron

1269
00:50:48,079 --> 00:50:52,079
communicates with the next cell, often

1270
00:50:49,760 --> 00:50:54,079
through a syninnapse. There, chemical

1271
00:50:52,079 --> 00:50:55,920
messengers or direct electrical

1272
00:50:54,079 --> 00:50:57,760
connections pass the information

1273
00:50:55,920 --> 00:51:00,800
forward, continuing the chain of

1274
00:50:57,760 --> 00:51:02,800
processing in the nervous system.

1275
00:51:00,800 --> 00:51:05,040
This is the fundamental process behind

1276
00:51:02,800 --> 00:51:07,280
everything from reflexes to complex

1277
00:51:05,040 --> 00:51:09,359
thought. And it's also the biological

1278
00:51:07,280 --> 00:51:11,839
inspiration for how artificial neural

1279
00:51:09,359 --> 00:51:14,839
networks process information in AI

1280
00:51:11,839 --> 00:51:14,839
systems.

1281
00:51:16,480 --> 00:51:20,079
Now, here is the simplest way to think

1282
00:51:18,400 --> 00:51:22,800
about it.

1283
00:51:20,079 --> 00:51:24,720
At the top, you see a biological neuron.

1284
00:51:22,800 --> 00:51:27,200
It receives input through many branches

1285
00:51:24,720 --> 00:51:29,040
called dendrites. All of these signals

1286
00:51:27,200 --> 00:51:30,800
are gathered in the main cell body, the

1287
00:51:29,040 --> 00:51:33,040
soma.

1288
00:51:30,800 --> 00:51:35,440
If the combined signal is strong enough,

1289
00:51:33,040 --> 00:51:38,400
the neuron generates an electrical pulse

1290
00:51:35,440 --> 00:51:40,400
that travels down the axon. Finally, it

1291
00:51:38,400 --> 00:51:42,800
reaches the output interface, the

1292
00:51:40,400 --> 00:51:45,440
syninnapse, where it passes the signal

1293
00:51:42,800 --> 00:51:47,520
onto other neurons.

1294
00:51:45,440 --> 00:51:50,240
Below that is the mathematical model we

1295
00:51:47,520 --> 00:51:52,640
use for an artificial neuron.

1296
00:51:50,240 --> 00:51:54,400
Each input is represented as a variable

1297
00:51:52,640 --> 00:51:56,160
and not all inputs carry the same

1298
00:51:54,400 --> 00:51:58,559
importance. So, we assign a weight to

1299
00:51:56,160 --> 00:52:00,480
each one. Larger weights mean that input

1300
00:51:58,559 --> 00:52:02,800
has a bigger influence. Smaller weights

1301
00:52:00,480 --> 00:52:04,640
mean less influence.

1302
00:52:02,800 --> 00:52:06,880
The neuron first performs a linear

1303
00:52:04,640 --> 00:52:08,960
operation, a weighted sum of all the

1304
00:52:06,880 --> 00:52:11,680
inputs, which is essentially an inner

1305
00:52:08,960 --> 00:52:13,440
product. But that's not enough. Just

1306
00:52:11,680 --> 00:52:16,480
like in biology, small random

1307
00:52:13,440 --> 00:52:18,480
fluctuations, small nudges are ignored.

1308
00:52:16,480 --> 00:52:20,000
Only when the total input crosses a

1309
00:52:18,480 --> 00:52:22,160
certain threshold does the neuron

1310
00:52:20,000 --> 00:52:24,160
respond strongly. This is where the

1311
00:52:22,160 --> 00:52:27,040
nonlinear transformation comes in

1312
00:52:24,160 --> 00:52:29,760
producing the actual output.

1313
00:52:27,040 --> 00:52:32,079
So in short, first we sum the inputs in

1314
00:52:29,760 --> 00:52:33,839
a weighted way. Then we pass the result

1315
00:52:32,079 --> 00:52:36,000
through a nonlinear function that

1316
00:52:33,839 --> 00:52:39,000
decides whether to respond and how

1317
00:52:36,000 --> 00:52:39,000
strongly.

1318
00:52:40,720 --> 00:52:44,400
Now let's look at how we represent a

1319
00:52:42,480 --> 00:52:46,400
neuron in a computer. Uh what we call a

1320
00:52:44,400 --> 00:52:48,559
perceptron.

1321
00:52:46,400 --> 00:52:51,839
A perceptron takes multiple inputs each

1322
00:52:48,559 --> 00:52:55,680
labeled here as a 1, a 2, a 3, a n. Each

1323
00:52:51,839 --> 00:52:57,920
input has a weight shown as w1, w2, w3,

1324
00:52:55,680 --> 00:52:59,839
wn, which controls how important that

1325
00:52:57,920 --> 00:53:01,680
input is.

1326
00:52:59,839 --> 00:53:03,920
The first thing we do is multiply each

1327
00:53:01,680 --> 00:53:05,920
input by its weight. Then we sum them

1328
00:53:03,920 --> 00:53:08,640
all together. This is an inner product

1329
00:53:05,920 --> 00:53:10,880
operation. Often we also add an extra

1330
00:53:08,640 --> 00:53:13,280
term called a bias B which shifts the

1331
00:53:10,880 --> 00:53:15,520
output. You can think of the bias as an

1332
00:53:13,280 --> 00:53:17,440
offset, a way to control the baseline

1333
00:53:15,520 --> 00:53:19,680
response of the neuron even if all the

1334
00:53:17,440 --> 00:53:21,839
inputs are zero.

1335
00:53:19,680 --> 00:53:23,839
Once we have this weighted sum, we pass

1336
00:53:21,839 --> 00:53:26,079
it through a nonlinear function which we

1337
00:53:23,839 --> 00:53:29,520
usually call the activation function.

1338
00:53:26,079 --> 00:53:31,280
Here it's labeled sigma. This step is

1339
00:53:29,520 --> 00:53:35,440
essential. Without it, the perceptron

1340
00:53:31,280 --> 00:53:36,800
would just be a simple linear device.

1341
00:53:35,440 --> 00:53:39,280
There are many choices for the

1342
00:53:36,800 --> 00:53:41,040
activation function.

1343
00:53:39,280 --> 00:53:43,599
A common one is the sigmoid, which

1344
00:53:41,040 --> 00:53:45,839
produces an S-shaped curve. Another is

1345
00:53:43,599 --> 00:53:48,720
the hyperbolic tangent or tan, which

1346
00:53:45,839 --> 00:53:50,480
gives outputs between minus1 and + one.

1347
00:53:48,720 --> 00:53:52,400
There are also peace-wise linear

1348
00:53:50,480 --> 00:53:54,720
functions such as the realu the

1349
00:53:52,400 --> 00:53:56,800
rectified linear unit where the output

1350
00:53:54,720 --> 00:53:58,880
is zero for negative inputs and

1351
00:53:56,800 --> 00:54:00,720
increases proportionally for positive

1352
00:53:58,880 --> 00:54:03,359
inputs.

1353
00:54:00,720 --> 00:54:06,079
So in short a perceptron takes weighted

1354
00:54:03,359 --> 00:54:08,400
inputs adds them up applies a bias and

1355
00:54:06,079 --> 00:54:10,800
then uses a nonlinear transformation to

1356
00:54:08,400 --> 00:54:12,720
produce its output. This artificial

1357
00:54:10,800 --> 00:54:14,880
neuron is the basic building block for

1358
00:54:12,720 --> 00:54:17,200
artificial neural networks. Just as

1359
00:54:14,880 --> 00:54:21,640
resistors, capacitors and inductors are

1360
00:54:17,200 --> 00:54:21,640
building blocks in electrical circuits.

1361
00:54:23,280 --> 00:54:26,880
Now that we understand a single

1362
00:54:24,800 --> 00:54:29,040
perceptron, let's see what happens when

1363
00:54:26,880 --> 00:54:31,760
we connect many of them. This gives us

1364
00:54:29,040 --> 00:54:33,760
an artificial neural network.

1365
00:54:31,760 --> 00:54:35,680
At the far left, we have the input

1366
00:54:33,760 --> 00:54:37,839
layer. Each circle here receives one

1367
00:54:35,680 --> 00:54:39,599
piece of information from our data.

1368
00:54:37,839 --> 00:54:41,280
These could be pixel values from an

1369
00:54:39,599 --> 00:54:42,960
image, measurements from a sensor, or

1370
00:54:41,280 --> 00:54:46,480
any other kind of features we want the

1371
00:54:42,960 --> 00:54:49,040
network to process.

1372
00:54:46,480 --> 00:54:51,200
Next, we have one or more hidden layers.

1373
00:54:49,040 --> 00:54:53,280
Each neuron in a hidden layer takes the

1374
00:54:51,200 --> 00:54:55,839
outputs from the previous layer, applies

1375
00:54:53,280 --> 00:54:58,319
its weights, sums them up, passes the

1376
00:54:55,839 --> 00:55:00,319
result through its activation function,

1377
00:54:58,319 --> 00:55:02,480
and then sends the output to the next

1378
00:55:00,319 --> 00:55:04,800
layer. These hidden layers are where the

1379
00:55:02,480 --> 00:55:07,599
network learns increasingly complex

1380
00:55:04,800 --> 00:55:09,280
patterns.

1381
00:55:07,599 --> 00:55:12,160
Finally, at the far right, we have the

1382
00:55:09,280 --> 00:55:14,160
output layer. In a classification task,

1383
00:55:12,160 --> 00:55:16,559
each neuron here might represent a

1384
00:55:14,160 --> 00:55:18,800
possible label. For example, dog, cat,

1385
00:55:16,559 --> 00:55:20,800
or car. The neuron with the highest

1386
00:55:18,800 --> 00:55:22,640
output value would be the network's

1387
00:55:20,800 --> 00:55:25,440
prediction.

1388
00:55:22,640 --> 00:55:28,640
Here's the key idea. A single neuron can

1389
00:55:25,440 --> 00:55:30,800
only separate very simple patterns.

1390
00:55:28,640 --> 00:55:33,839
By stacking many layers, the network can

1391
00:55:30,800 --> 00:55:36,079
build up a hierarchy of features.

1392
00:55:33,839 --> 00:55:38,640
The first layer might detect basic edges

1393
00:55:36,079 --> 00:55:41,200
or colors. The next layer might detect

1394
00:55:38,640 --> 00:55:43,200
shapes like wheels or ears. Higher

1395
00:55:41,200 --> 00:55:45,839
layers combine these into entire objects

1396
00:55:43,200 --> 00:55:47,920
like a car or a cat.

1397
00:55:45,839 --> 00:55:49,680
Training the network works like this. We

1398
00:55:47,920 --> 00:55:52,720
start with random weights. So the

1399
00:55:49,680 --> 00:55:54,640
predictions are essentially guesses.

1400
00:55:52,720 --> 00:55:56,640
We compare the network's output to the

1401
00:55:54,640 --> 00:55:58,720
correct answer and compute the error.

1402
00:55:56,640 --> 00:56:01,119
Then using a process called back

1403
00:55:58,720 --> 00:56:03,119
propagation, we send this error backward

1404
00:56:01,119 --> 00:56:05,280
through the network, adjusting the

1405
00:56:03,119 --> 00:56:06,880
weight slightly to reduce the error next

1406
00:56:05,280 --> 00:56:08,880
time.

1407
00:56:06,880 --> 00:56:10,720
With enough data, enough layers, and

1408
00:56:08,880 --> 00:56:13,280
many training cycles, the network learns

1409
00:56:10,720 --> 00:56:15,040
to recognize very complex patterns, the

1410
00:56:13,280 --> 00:56:17,280
kind of capability that powers things

1411
00:56:15,040 --> 00:56:21,400
like self-driving cars, medical image

1412
00:56:17,280 --> 00:56:21,400
analysis, and voice recognition.

1413
00:56:23,280 --> 00:56:27,599
Once you have the basic idea of how a

1414
00:56:25,520 --> 00:56:29,359
